  "basis": "pack",
  "notes": [
    "material_intensity_kg_per_kwh is expressed per kWh of RATED (nameplate) energy at PACK level, i.e. it already includes busbars, enclosure and module hardware.",
    "Only economically payable elements are listed. Everything else in the pack (separator, binder, electrolyte solvent, plastics, wiring insulation) is treated as inert mass by the BOM builder and carries no recovery revenue.",
    "These are indicative industry defaults used ONLY when a passport does not declare its own composition. EU Regulation 2023/1542 Annex XIII requires declaration of cobalt, lithium, nickel and lead content, so for a compliant passport the declared values take precedence.",
    "Elements use IUPAC symbols. 'C' denotes anode graphite specifically.",
    "typical_cycle_life_to_80pct is full equivalent cycles to 80% state of health under typical automotive duty. It sets the denominator for remaining-life estimates when a passport gives cycle count but no state of health."
  ],
  "sources": [
    "Argonne National Laboratory, BatPaC v5 battery pack design model",
    "IEA, Global EV Outlook - critical mineral intensity of EV batteries",
    "Transport & Environment, 'From dirty oil to clean batteries' material demand modelling",
    "EU Regulation 2023/1542, Annex XIII (passport data) and Annex XII (recycling efficiency)"
  ],
